## Week 2: Automatic Data Cleaning

### My Role
Data and Backend Developer

### Work Completed
- Handled missing product descriptions and country values.
- Removed records missing essential transaction information.
- Replaced missing customer IDs with a consistent placeholder.
- Removed duplicate sales records.
- Standardised customer IDs and cleaned text columns.
- Validated the cleaned dataset.
- Added a cleaning summary showing original rows, processed rows, removed rows, duplicates dropped and missing values handled.
- Tested the cleaning process in the Streamlit application.

### Challenges
I encountered an error because the cleaning summary expected a `missing_values_handled` value that was not initially included in the pipeline statistics. I updated the statistics and restarted Streamlit to resolve the issue.

### What I Learned
I learned how to handle different types of missing data, remove duplicate records, standardise data formats and display cleaning results clearly in a Streamlit application.

### Outcome
The application successfully cleans uploaded sales data and displays a clear summary of the changes made.
